 When a ceiling is reached TA stops the agent, prints which ceiling and what was used, records the outcome `aborted_budget` on the goal, and builds the draft from the partial work, marked as incomplete (`ta draft view` says so first). What it can promise: TA reads the runtime's usage report after each agent turn, so the agent is stopped at the first turn boundary after the ceiling is crossed. Overshoot is possible by up to one turn (a single long turn can cost a lot); undershoot is capped, since a goal is never stopped before it reaches the ceiling. Ceilings are enforced only for headless runs, because that is where TA reads the usage report. `--max-usd` needs a price: from the runtime's reported cost or the price table. For an unpriced model it warns and only `--max-tokens` applies. A goal that finishes on its own over the ceiling is not marked incomplete.
 
+### Spend across goals and interactive sessions
+
+`GET /api/spend` only sees TA goals. `ta cost report` adds the interactive Claude Code and OMP sessions you run by hand, which are often the larger cost:
+
+```bash
+ta cost report                                   # totals by source, plus the context-size table
+ta cost report --group-by day --since 2026-10-01 # per day since a date
+ta cost report --group-by model,project --json   # machine-readable
+ta cost report --project TrustedAutonomy         # one project only
+ta cost report --group-by context_bucket         # spend by context size
+```
+
+Sources are detected automatically and each is optional: this project's TA goals, Claude Code sessions in `~/.claude/projects`, and OMP sessions in `~/.omp/agent/sessions`. A source that is missing is named in the header, not treated as an error. Use `--claude-dir` or `--omp-dir` if your sessions live elsewhere.
+
+Flags: `--since` and `--until` (RFC 3339 or `YYYY-MM-DD`, UTC, `--until` exclusive), `--project` (directory name of the session's working directory), `--group-by` with any of `day`, `source`, `model`, `project`, `context_bucket`, `origin_class` (comma separated to combine), and `--json`.
+
+Example output (trimmed):
+
+```
+Sources
+  [missing] ta_goal      .../.ta/goals does not exist. Run this from a TA project to include its goals.
+  [found]   claude_code  /Users/me/.claude/projects (107 files, 6,259 records)
+  [found]   omp          /Users/me/.omp/agent/sessions (133 files, 12,147 records)
+Claude rows read: 11,932; duplicate rows collapsed: 5,673; synthetic rows skipped: 2; malformed lines: 0; unreadable files: 0
+Costs: $24.77 estimated (259 records), $387.00 exact (12147 records), 6000 unpriced (no price for the model)
+Unpriced models (tokens counted, usd 0): claude-sonnet-5 (6,000). Add rows to .ta/pricing.toml to price them.
+
+By context size (transcript turns; goals have no per-turn context)
+  source       context      turns   cache rd         usd   share
+  claude_code  100-200k       987     141.8M      $14.92   60.2%
+  claude_code  200-400k     1,569     457.4M       $5.35   21.6%
+```
+
+How the numbers are made:
+
+- **No double counting.** Claude Code writes several rows for one message; they are collapsed by message id (the last row wins) and `<synthetic>` rows are skipped. The header says how many rows were collapsed.
+- **Exact or estimated.** OMP and runtime-reported goal costs are exact. Claude Code transcripts do not carry a cost, so theirs is estimated from the price table (`.ta/pricing.toml` over the built-in rows). Cache writes the transcript marks as 1 hour are priced at 2x the input rate. A model with no price row costs 0 and is listed under "Unpriced models"; TA never invents a price. The provisional Claude 5 rows can be off by about 2x, so compare token counts when it matters.
+- **Context size.** A turn's context is its whole prompt: uncached input plus cache read plus cache write. The table shows turns, cache-read tokens and cost for 0-50k, 50-100k, 100-200k, 200-400k and 400k+, per source. Long sessions spend most of their money in the top buckets because every turn re-reads the whole context.
